WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.490
Dim Sum Rush. A partnership climbing game

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.740
where you help your partner through the face-up tiles you share.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.010
Lead a single, a set like five-five, or a run like three-four-five.

4
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.650
Others must follow with the same kind and size,

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.490
of equal or higher ranks, or pass.

6
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.360
You can't rearrange your hand. Teammates help you through the trolley:

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.480
when you pass, swap an end tile for one, and slide it in anywhere.

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.470
Teams sit alternating.

9
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.320
Everyone on the team must empty their hands to win the round.

10
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.730
I lead three-four-five from my hand.

11
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.960
Bao beats it.

12
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.620
My partner passes, putting out an eight.

13
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:38.500
I pass and swap the two at the end of my hand for her eight.

14
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.510
She goes out on three tens.

15
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.540
Six to nine from my hand: a Chef's Special, which beats any ordinary play.

16
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.010
Our side is out, so their team takes penalty points.

17
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.170
Two to six players, thirty to forty-five minutes.

18
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.960
The fewest penalties after three rounds wins.

19
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.350
There's also a free-for-all mode where everyone just plays for themselves,

20
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.310
sharing a trolley with their neighbors to the left and right.

21
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:03.970
Dim Sum Rush.

22
00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:08.080
Play it in your browser at darrendon.com, or email me for a prototype.
